  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 309 AM EDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\n- Small chances of showers/storms through Friday; Mainly South\n\nAs has been the case the past couple of days, the main ring of fire \nconvection axis has remained south of our forecast area. This is the \nresult of the stalled out boundary keeping the very hot and humid \nconditions well south of the state, and the sfc waves riding along \nit.\n\nThe models continue to show at least a couple of additional clusters \nof storms just missing us to the south again. Based on the pattern \nthe last couple of days without any big push northward, this seems \nvery likely. Especially with another weak front dropping south \nthrough the area early this morning. Can not rule out some rain \nalong the far southern edge of the forecast area on the northern \nedge of any cluster. \n\n- Periods of showers/storms likely Friday night into Sunday\n\nWe do see some changes in the pattern showing up beginning Friday \nnight, and lasting into Sunday. This change in the pattern is \nfacilitated by a long wave trough taking hold over the Western third \nof the country. This wave then ejects a couple of short waves and \nsends them via a more SW flow aloft toward the area.\n\nThis pattern shift then also pushes the boundary further north, \nbringing the higher heat and humidity closer to the area. With short \nwaves riding along this front, we will see MCS activity ramp up once \nagain with the associated low level jets traversing over our \nsouthern area, or staying just south and the nose of them aiming \ntoward the area. We will need to keep an eye on this as we could see \nstrong to severe storms be possible while we are under the theta e \naxis and short wave train.\n\nThis really looks possible from Friday evening all the way into \nSunday. On Sunday, we see a general trend in the pattern showing \nthat everything sinks south as the SW flow aloft and upper ridge \ngets flattened a bit. This includes the baroclinic zone and active \nzone for MCS activity, along with cooler weather filtering in. \n\n- Cooling off and drying out Monday through most of Wednesday\n\nThe front will sink south through the area no later than Sunday, \ntaking with it the moisture and instability, and shunting it to our \nsouth by Monday. Upper and sfc ridging will build in for Monday \nthrough at least early Wednesday, keeping us dry. There are some \nindications the next wave could come in late next Wednesday. We have \ntime to fine tune the timing of this.",
